  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1045 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nThe passing wave will force another frontal boundary through the\nregion Thursday night into Friday bringing reinforcing shot of\ncooler air into the region for the weekend. Mostly cloudy skies,\nespecially across the north on Friday will likely keep highs in\nthe 50s for many locations. some light drizzle or sprinkles could\nalso be possible during the day Friday before skies begin to clear\nby mid to late afternoon. Surface high pressure will settle over\nthe region through the weekend leading to some cool nights.\nLocations across the north could dip into the 30s both Saturday\nand Sunday morning, with a few of the normally colder spots\npossibly dropping to near freezing. \n\nTemperatures begin to rebound by late weekend into next week as\nsurface ridging shifts east and southerly flow returns to the\nregion. Highs will climb back above normal for early next week as\nthe forecast will remain dry for now after Thursday. A couple of \nweak waves will pass near the region and could bring some chances \nfor more showers through next week, but chances are too low to \nmention at this point.\n\nBowlan",
